-- coa29-sch2-part3.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46, SCHEDULE 2, PART 3 "Overseas regulatory bodies".
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Generated by work/build.py from work/src/coa29-sch2-part3.l4; quote lines are produced by srcrefs.py.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Line numbers are of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- TARGET. The stable `l4` (main) 1.6.110.
--
-- WHAT THIS PART DOES. Section 948(3)(d) (coa21) says the bar on the Takeover Panel's disclosure of information about an individual or a
-- business does not apply to a disclosure "made in accordance with Part 3 of that Schedule". Paragraph 1 says when a disclosure to an overseas
-- regulator is so made; paragraph 2 says what the Panel must have regard to in deciding whether to make it. "The British Islands" is not
-- defined in these sources: whether a country or territory is outside them is a plain input. "Appear to the Panel" is the Panel's judgment: it
-- is an input, never guessed (Guide section 4).
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is within the provision; JUST FALSE =
-- the text says no in its own words (an unmet "if", a definition by "are", a bare "must" not done); NOTHING = the text does not decide.

§ `Schedule 2 -- Part 3: overseas regulatory bodies`

-- What the Panel does under para 2: it has regard to the considerations. A typed action for the regulative rule below.
DECLARE `sch 2 part 3 action of the Panel` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 part 3 have regard to the considerations in paragraph 2`

-- src:19327 | (2) “Relevant functions” for this purpose are functions of a public nature that appear to the Panel to be similar to its own functions or those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority or similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England.
@ref sch 2 part 3 para 1(2) Relevant functions (src:19327)
GIVEN `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 part 3 para 1(2) the functions are relevant functions` MEANS
    IF       `the functions are functions of a public nature`
         AND (   `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions`
              OR `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority`
              OR `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant functions” for this purpose are functions of a public nature that appear to the Panel to be similar to its own functions or those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority or similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England"

-- src:19324 | 1 (1) A disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule if—
-- src:19325 | (a) it is made to a person or body exercising relevant functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands, and
-- src:19326 | (b) it is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions.
@ref sch 2 part 3 para 1(1) A disclosure made in accordance with this Part (src:19324-19326)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the functions are functions of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 part 3 para 1(1) the disclosure is made in accordance with this Part` MEANS
    IF       `the disclosure is made to a person or body exercising functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands`
         AND `sch 2 part 3 para 1(2) the functions are relevant functions` `the functions are functions of a public nature` `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the Panel's own functions` `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority` `it appears to the Panel that the functions are similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         AND `the disclosure is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure is made in accordance with this Part of this Schedule if— (a) it is made to a person or body exercising relevant functions under legislation in a country or territory outside the British Islands, and (b) it is made for the purpose of enabling or assisting that person or body to exercise those functions" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))

-- Para 2: the Panel MUST have regard to the considerations. The text gives no time, so no WITHIN is written. The decision twin follows.
-- src:19328 | 2 In determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part of this Schedule, the Panel must have regard to the following considerations—
-- src:19329 | (a) whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure;
-- src:19330 | (b) whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed, otherwise than—
-- src:19331 | (i) for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a), or
-- src:19332 | (ii) for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed.
@ref sch 2 part 3 para 2 The Panel must have regard to the considerations (src:19328-19332)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sch 2 part 3 action of the Panel`
`sch 2 part 3 para 2 the Panel must have regard to the considerations before disclosing to an overseas body` MEANS
    PARTY `Takeover Panel`
    MUST `sch 2 part 3 have regard to the considerations in paragraph 2`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Takeover Panel` BECAUSE "the Panel did not have regard to whether the use the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify the disclosure, and whether it has adequate arrangements to prevent the information being used or further disclosed"

@ref sch 2 part 3 para 2 The Panel must have regard to the considerations (src:19328-19332)
GIVEN `the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 part 3 para 2 the Panel has had regard to the considerations` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the Panel is determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether to disclose information to a person or body in accordance with this Part of this Schedule, the Panel must have regard to the following considerations"
    ELSE IF       `the Panel has had regard to whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure`
              AND `the Panel has had regard to whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed otherwise than for the purposes of carrying out the functions mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) or for other purposes substantially similar to those for which information disclosed to the Panel could be used or further disclosed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Panel must have regard to the following considerations— (a) whether the use that the person or body is likely to make of the information is sufficiently important to justify making the disclosure; (b) whether the person or body has adequate arrangements to prevent the information from being used or further disclosed" (a bare "must" not done: fork)
